# MCSP Driver Construction Fixture 0.56

Status: Constructive driver-construction experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parents:
- DMA-TRANSFER-PROJECTION-0.34.mcsp
- QEMU EDU DMA witness 0.35
- DRIVER-BUILDER-INTERFACE-0.52.mcsp
- KBUILD-MODULE-INTEGRATION-0.54.mcsp
- KERNEL-DRIVER-BUILDER-REPORT-0.55.mcsp

## Foundational direction

MCSP is itself a kernel:

    MCSP KERNEL = DETERMINATE CONDITION

The MCSP kernel determines semantic obligations. A driver builder consumes the
resulting report. Linux is a downstream external realization kernel when selected.

## Objective

Demonstrate a bounded report-driven construction of a Linux PCI driver artifact for
the QEMU EDU device witness without loading the driver or touching hardware.

QEMU EDU identification used by the established witness:

    vendor = 0x1234
    device = 0x11e8

The identification values locate the bounded hardware applicability. They do not
define MCSP semantics.

## Construction

    MCSP KERNEL
      -> QEMU EDU boundary obligation
      -> driver-builder report
      -> builder projection
      -> MCSP assembly-owned probe predicate
      -> Linux PCI registration adapter
      -> Kbuild
      -> .ko
      -> static disassembly / symbol / metadata verification
      -> REALIZE / SUSPEND / REJECT

## Bounded report obligations

- hardware boundary: PCI;
- vendor 0x1234;
- device 0x11e8;
- transfer capability: DMA witness exists;
- access realization: Linux PCI;
- no interrupt requirement in this construction fixture;
- no DMA execution in this construction fixture;
- no MMIO access in this construction fixture;
- semantic mutation forbidden;
- STATE and TYPE not required;
- unresolved incompatibility suspends construction.

## Assembly ownership

The MCSP assembly component exposes:

    mcsp_edu_identity_match

Input projection:
    RDI = vendor
    RSI = device

Output projection:
    RAX = 1 only for 0x1234:0x11e8, otherwise 0.

This is a bounded construction predicate derived from the report. It does not probe
PCI configuration space itself.

## Linux adapter

The Linux adapter registers a PCI driver table for the bounded EDU identity and
calls the MCSP predicate during probe. It performs no MMIO, DMA, interrupt setup,
or device mutation.

## Boundary

0.56 produces a driver-shaped Linux module artifact but does not load it.
Actual PCI probing, binding, hardware access, DMA, interrupt operation, unload
behavior, recovery, and production safety remain unverified.
